      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI'm focusing on crafting a Python script, `presigned_download.py`, to generate time-limited, signed URLs. My central decision right now is selecting AWS S3 as the object storage provider for this functionality.\n\n\n**Implementing the Core Logic**\n\nI've decided to proceed with AWS S3 and `boto3`. My current focus is on building the `create_presigned_download_url` function within `presigned_download.py`. This function will handle the URL generation, taking the bucket name, object name (key), and expiration time as inputs. The script needs to effectively utilize boto3's S3 client to produce the required pre-signed URL.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789821161595,
          "start": 1789821159580
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a7889c001t7wf4BueGfHark",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a783a3001x7swfJAsZkwcrz",
      "session_id": "ses_f46587c72ffeyMMQdW6460DUwM",
      "time_created": 1789821159580,
      "time_updated": 1789821161596
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tmNqU0BUXBRKxMgB",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ndef create_presigned_download_url(bucket_name: str, object_name: str, expiration: int = 3600):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate a presigned URL to download an S3 object\n\n    :param bucket_name: Name of the S3 bucket\n    :param object_name: Key of the S3 object\n    :param expiration: Time in seconds for the presigned URL to remain valid\n    :return: Presigned URL as string. If error, returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    s3_client = boto3.client('s3')\n    try:\n        response = s3_client.generate_presigned_url('get_object',\n                                                    Params={'Bucket': bucket_name,\n                                                            'Key': object_name},\n                                                    ExpiresIn=expiration)\n    except ClientError as e:\n        print(f\"Error creating presigned URL: {e}\")\n        return None\n    return response\n",
            "filePath": "presigned_download.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
            "filepath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-ye8qgrlh/presigned_download.py",
